<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n38669" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπεντύω</span></b>  and <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπεν-ύνω</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ῡν</span>], <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>set right, get ready,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπέντυε νῶϊν ἵππους</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					8.374
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χεῖρα ἐπεντύνειν ἐπί τινι</span>
			<i>arm</i> it for the fight, v.l. in
			<i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Aj.</u>
				451
			</span></i>:—
				Med.
			, <i>prepare</i> or <i>train oneself for</i> a thing, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπεντύνονται ἄεθλα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					24.89
				</span></i>
			: c. inf., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπεντύνοντο νέεσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.R.
					1.720
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
